This [[Gender|male]] '''[[Ugnaught]]''' worked as a vendor in the [[Colossus marketplace|marketplace]] of the ''[[Colossus]]'' platform on [[Castilon]],<ref name="The High Tower" /> selling [[Foodstuff|food]].<ref name="The Children from Tehar">{{Resistance|The Children from Tehar}}</ref> He was generally unpleasant with his customers, refusing to allow them to purchase more than one bowl of his wares. The vendor had a bushy grey beard and a peg leg.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

While going inside before curfew when the platform was experiencing a power outage, he was briefly harassed by [[speagull]]s, before informing [[Kazuda Xiono]] of the curfew.<ref name="The High Tower" /> Later, while he was distracted arguing with a customer, [[Garma]], young fugitives [[Kel]] and [[Eila]] took the opportunity to steal a bowl of food to eat. When he discovered it missing, the vendor tracked the children down and chased them around the market. The children eventually came to the end of the marketplace where [[Bolza Grool]]'s stall was located, leading the vendor to, while leaping off a stack of crates, collide with Grool and knock them both over. One of Grool's [[gorg]]s fell on the vendor's face, and he had difficulty pulling it off, as the children escaped.<ref name="The Children from Tehar" />

{{Char-stub}}

==Behind the scenes==
The Ugnaught vendor is a character on ''[[Star Wars Resistance]]'', and is voiced by franchise regular [[Dee Bradley Baker]].

